    "umvpa-wave3-independent-review-20260930": {
      "body": "Approve M2.03 candidate commit 4f52d15fb72493dabeac20914604a07275663d31 against base 4d2463b82c3546fa44bbddcb3b83f4c037e32b1b. Independently reviewed the query implementation and the oracle mathematical expectations and code authored by query_oracles; I did not author those oracles or execute these builds. No remaining blocking findings in the reviewed M2 scope.\n\nConfirmed candidate identity, clean canonical checkout, source-manifest canonical entry, and SHA256 parity for all three candidate paths with the source previously reviewed. Query source SHA256 1f9bd14f7efe239983d8ce4dcc902b2391f260af587bd7a58e2e687ae3ec5e45; oracle SHA256 a1229032af655154f5c6e8948b37f991fcc0fbf5bf9683529d847faaed8c6dfe; verification document SHA256 43c7011031e991b775e6f0503b2b775c184def3c19ad40fc3b0af0e7770c1557.\n\nReviewed retained complete execution logs and matching meta.json receipts from the canonical checkout, with log byte lengths verified: mvpaJVM/test 205 passed, 0 failed/errors; mvpaJS/test 205 passed, 0 failed/errors; scalafimCompileAll exit 0 and no warnings/errors in its full log. All three receipts report exit_code=0 and child_returncode=0. Log SHA256 respectively 882616a4994bbd38527dee70b6329a7089da4bd43e1d03eea27a92b6edab2537, ccd9e3ebeddaf5da3fc5562c863dc434f53f8551d91bfc7294a9f9c0a63ff186, 04354c41fa7c1348e5a286de7f4c36e3bb5ab2661ddc9c754a48c55a6146a095.\n\nEvidence covers rectangular signed scalar/form agreement, actual backward adjoints, pair reversal, nominal axes, lazy opening, one-shot scalar refusal, width-one operator execution and scale-aware contractions. Approval is a candidate review only: it grants no landing authorization, resolves no pending ancestor, and makes no upstream Alder publication/pin or M1.06 qualification claim.\n\nInspected source and execution receipt paths:\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/source-manifest.json\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/wave3-canonical-mvpa-jvm.log\n/private/tmp/s